id: pm-blvfye
title: "GH-1118: natural-language word-number titles trigger duplicate issue-code false positives"
description: "The duplicate issue-code title heuristic treats prose such as Match-3, Covid-19, or Wi-Fi-6 as tracker identifiers and emits an impossible rename-or-merge remediation for unrelated items."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:governance","area:validate",false-positive,github-intake
created_at: "2026-08-25T16:27:05.142Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-26T16:57:30.085Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-26T16:57:29.548Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-26T16:57:29.548Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The classifier distinguishes prose compounds from evidence-backed issue identifiers without maintaining an unbounded dictionary; negative controls retain detection for real uppercase and configured code formats; validation output explains the evidence and recovery path; focused tests cover Match-3, Covid-19, Wi-Fi-6, real codes, mixed case, body evidence, and configured formats; the full validation and 100 percent coverage gates pass."
parent: pm-33cw
risk: medium
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub issue #1118
severity: medium
repro_steps: "Create two unrelated items whose titles contain the same natural-language word-number token such as Match-3, then run pm validate --check-metadata."
resolution: Replaced shape-only word-number classification with evidence-backed issue-code recognition and normalized configured prefixes.
expected_result: "Natural compounds do not create duplicate-code findings while uppercase, delimited, configured, and body-cited real identifiers remain detected."
actual_result: "Match-3, Covid-19, and Wi-Fi-6 are excluded; real codes and configured prefixes with optional trailing hyphens are preserved under focused, full-coverage, and defect-evidence gates."
affected_version: 2026.8.23
component: metadata validation
