comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-25T16:27:05.142Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: strict-read inspected all 2,558 items across every lifecycle state with no omissions; searches for GH-1118, duplicate_issue_codes, Match-3, natural-language genre, and hyphenated word-number found adjacent historical false-positive work but no owner for prose compounds. Canonical source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1118"
  "2026-08-26T15:49:45.261Z","harness:codex","Final fix evidence: the duplicate issue-code classifier now rejects Match-3, Covid-19, Wi-Fi-6, and other prose compounds unless uppercase, configured-prefix, delimiter, or body-citation evidence establishes identifier intent. True GitHub/project identifiers remain detected. Focused 23-case classifier coverage, command validation, final exact 8,011-test 100/100/100/100 coverage, and full static quality pass; GH-1118 will close through the reviewed PR."
  "2026-08-26T16:06:48.848Z","harness:codex","Exact-head governance remediation: PR #1123 release:gates correctly failed closed because this post-epoch production defect lacked escape_class and structured gate_evidence. Added production_defect classification and bound the fix to the duplicate-issue-code-evidence-classification gate: prose-compound negative controls, true-identifier controls, focused local tests, defect-evidence gate, exact coverage, and hosted static/coverage owners. No waiver is used."
  "2026-08-26T16:57:17.648Z","harness:codex","PR review remediation evidence: configured issue-code prefixes are normalized with or without trailing separators, preserving evidence-backed detection while natural word-number compounds remain excluded. Focused validation tests, exact coverage, repository static quality, and defect-evidence gates passed."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-26T15:49:42.248Z","harness:codex","Issue-code extraction needs structural evidence, not hyphen shape alone: uppercase/configured prefixes, explicit delimiters, or body citations distinguish identifiers from natural-language compounds."
